1. The appellant herein, who is the petitioner in the Court below, by way of this appeal under
Section 39
of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 (for brevity 'the Act'), seeks to assail the order dated 5.4.2007 in I.A. No. 850 of 2007 in O.P. No. 338 of 2007 on the file of the Court of First Additional District Judge at Khammam, dismissing an interim injunction application purported to be filed under
Section 9(ii)(d)
of the Act, whereunder the appellant sought an ad interim injunction restraining the respondents from deducting any amount from the running bills of the appellant in respect of Purchase Order No. KC-60 & ROC. 1030, dated 30.6.2006 unilaterally pending disposal of the main O.P. 3. The appellant herein filed the main application in O.P. No. 338 of 2007 against the respondents herein with the following reliefs:
